40,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found that chasing money for individual sessions takes six hours a month, while yearly collection takes only one. Also, mid-year joiners each need a manual calculation, which seems like a lot of extra work.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial records show that seventy percent of our costs are fixed overheads, regardless of attendance. Additionally, a third of renewals were delayed, with some members requesting monthly payments. We cannot ignore these fixed costs or the payment struggles.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My research shows that many potential members are deterred by the commitment of a full year's fee upfront. Furthermore, past attempts at tiered grades caused friction and discouraged those in lower tiers from participating.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,May,,"It's exactly as I feared. Turnout for weekday meetings dropped by a third after we started charging at the door; people stopped feeling like those nights belonged to them. Plus, some members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My suspicions were correct. A mere quarter of the members account for two-thirds of all attendance, and the same nine people are doing all the setup and locking up. We have a massive imbalance in both usage and labor.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if most costs are fixed, maybe a yearly fee is better? But @Minako, you said people hate paying for a whole year at once. I'm worried about the treasurer's time if we charge per event.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, you are correct. Charging per event would be a nightmare for the treasurer and risky for the club, given that seventy percent of our costs are fixed and must be paid regardless of turnout.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, I agree that fixed costs are a priority, but we must address the barrier to entry. If a large annual fee scares off newcomers and tiered systems create social friction, we need a balanced approach.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly! If we make it too expensive or rigid, we lose the soul of the club. But @Shunichi, if only a few people are coming, maybe they're the ones who feel the most pressure? We need to make it feel effortless again.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, it's not about pressure; it's about exploitation. A handful of us are doing all the work and using the facilities, while others pay the same and vanish. That's the imbalance that needs fixing.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I understand it feels unfair. But if we make the rules too complicated to fix that, the treasurer will spend all their time on paperwork instead of helping the club. We need something simple.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, simplicity is essential, but it must be grounded in financial reality. If we ignore the fixed costs or the fact that many struggle with lump sums, we are merely guessing again. We need a structure that secures our overheads.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shunichi, while I understand the frustration over imbalance, we must be careful. My findings show that tiered systems in the past created social divisions and discouraged members. We cannot sacrifice the club's unity for a perceived fairness.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minako, I'm with you. If we start categorizing people, it'll just feel like a hierarchy. We need to get rid of that ""pay-as-you-go"" hesitation and make everyone feel like they truly belong here again.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, unity is a fantasy if the people actually running the place feel resentful. We can't just ignore that eighteen people pay and never show up while nine of us do everything. That's not a community; it's a subsidy.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want us to find a way that doesn't make the treasurer quit. If chasing individual payments takes six hours a month, we should probably avoid that, regardless of who is attending.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, your point is critical. Between the high fixed costs and the administrative burden of session-based collection, a per-event system is logically unsound. We must prioritize a structure that ensures financial stability and operational efficiency.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, I agree that stability is key. However, we must also consider that a high upfront cost is a barrier for newcomers. We need a solution that is administratively simple but doesn't alienate potential members.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly. We can't just lock the door with a huge fee. But @Shunichi, if we make it too complex to be ""fair,"" we'll just kill the vibe entirely. We need something that feels welcoming and easy.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""easy"" for you is ""unfair"" for the people actually doing the work. If we just keep it simple and flat, we're just subsidizing the ghosts. We need a system that reflects actual usage.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
