65,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Looking at the options, Option B seems like it would be a nightmare for the treasurer. I think Option A is the simplest and safest for the person keeping the books.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, I agree. Option B is logically unsound given the high fixed costs and the administrative burden you discovered. Option A ensures our overheads are covered and minimizes the treasurer's workload.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, while Option A is simple, we must remember that a large upfront fee deters newcomers. However, Option C's tiered approach previously caused social friction and discouraged members. Between these, Option A is the least divisive.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,May,,"I agree with Minako. Option B is exactly what killed the vibe for the weekday meetings, and Option C sounds like a recipe for social cliques. Option A is the only way to make people feel they truly belong.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""belonging"" shouldn't mean the active few pay for the inactive many. Option A is just a subsidy for ghosts. However, Option B is a clerical disaster and Option C is a social minefield. I'll vote A, but I'm not happy.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I'm glad we can all agree on something. If even Shunichi thinks the other options are too problematic, then Option A really is the best way to keep the club running smoothly.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, it is the only rational choice. It secures our fixed costs and prevents the administrative collapse we've seen. While not perfect for everyone, it provides the stability the club needs to survive.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, I agree. While I still worry about the barrier for newcomers, the risk of social division with Option C is too high. Option A preserves the club's unity and simplicity, which are our greatest strengths.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,May,,Exactly! Let's just make it a flat fee and get back to the fun part. No more worrying about door charges or tiers—just one payment and everyone is welcome. I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, don't mistake my vote for enthusiasm. I'm choosing the lesser of three evils. If we go with A, we're ignoring the imbalance, but B and C are simply non-starters. I'm voting A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm really relieved we've found a solution that everyone can live with. It feels like the right choice for the club's future and the treasurer's sanity. I'm voting for Option A.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I concur. Given the evidence of high fixed costs and the administrative burden of other methods, Option A is the only sustainable path. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I agree. While it isn't perfect for newcomers, it avoids the social friction of tiers and the administrative chaos of per-event fees. For the sake of unity and stability, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,May,,I'm so happy we're all on the same page! Let's keep it simple and welcoming so everyone feels they belong. I'm definitely voting for Option A!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your enthusiasm is exhausting. But since we've all agreed that the alternatives are either a clerical nightmare or a social disaster, there's no point in arguing further. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm glad we could all agree. Let's hope this makes things easier for everyone next year. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for Option A. It is the most stable and rational choice to ensure our fixed costs are covered without overburdening the treasurer.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for Option A. It is the best way to maintain our club's welcoming atmosphere and avoid the divisions that tiered systems create.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for Option A! Let's get rid of the hesitation and make the club feel like a home for everyone again.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I vote for Option A. It's a flawed system that rewards the lazy, but it's better than the alternatives.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
